	<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
	<hr />

	<h2>What Personal Data Do We Collect and How?</h2>
	<p>Burial Helpline collects personal information in two main ways:</p>
	<p><strong>Information you provide directly:</strong> This may include personally identifying data, demographic information (such as age and state of residence), health-related data, and contact information. In most cases, our partners collect this information directly from you.</p>
	<p><strong>Automatically collected information:</strong> When you visit our site, we may automatically collect certain technical data such as your IP address, device information, browser type, and browsing history within the site.</p>

	<hr />

	<h2>Why Do We Process Your Data?</h2>
	<p>We process your personal information for the following purposes:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>To provide the services you requested and connect you with licensed insurance agents.</li>
		<li>To improve your experience on our website.</li>
		<li>To coordinate the delivery of your information to relevant partners and insurance providers.</li>
		<li>To provide customer support and respond to your inquiries.</li>
	</ul>

	<hr />

	<h2>How Long Do We Retain Your Personal Data?</h2>
	<p>We retain your personal information for as long as you use our services and for as long as necessary to comply with our legal obligations, resolve disputes, and enforce our agreements. Once the data is no longer needed for these purposes, we securely delete it.</p>

	<hr />

	<h2>How Do We Protect Your Personal Data?</h2>
	<p>We implement reasonable technical and organizational security measures to protect your personal information against unauthorized access, loss, or disclosure. However, no method of Internet transmission or electronic storage is 100% secure. While we strive to use commercially acceptable means to protect your information, we cannot guarantee its absolute security.</p>

	<hr />

	<h2>Who Do We Share Your Personal Data With?</h2>
	<p>We may share your personal information with the following categories of third parties:</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Service providers:</strong> Companies that help us operate our website and deliver services (e.g., technology, data analytics, customer support).</li>
		<li><strong>Business partners and insurers:</strong> Licensed agents and insurance companies that may offer you relevant products.</li>
		<li><strong>Government authorities:</strong> When required by applicable law.</li>
	</ul>
	<p><strong>Third-party websites:</strong> Our site may contain links to third-party websites. We are not responsible for the privacy practices of those sites and encourage you to review their privacy policies separately.</p>
	<p><strong>Mergers and acquisitions:</strong> In the event of a merger, acquisition, or asset sale, your personal information may be transferred as part of that transaction.</p>

	<hr />

	<h2>Do We Collect Information from Minors?</h2>
	<p>Our site is not directed at individuals under the age of 18, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from minors. If you are under 18, you should use this site only under the supervision of a parent or legal guardian.</p>

	<hr />

	<h2>What Are Your Rights?</h2>
	<p>Depending on your place of residence, you may have the following rights regarding your personal information:</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Access:</strong> Request a copy of the personal data we hold about you.</li>
		<li><strong>Correction:</strong> Request that we correct inaccurate or incomplete data.</li>
		<li><strong>Deletion:</strong> Request that we delete your personal information.</li>
		<li><strong>Portability:</strong> Receive your data in a structured, machine-readable format.</li>
		<li><strong>Opt-out:</strong> Opt out of receiving marketing communications or the sale of your data.</li>
		<li><strong>Non-discrimination:</strong> You will not be treated differently for exercising any of these rights.</li>
	</ul>

	<hr />

	<h2>How Can You Exercise Your Rights?</h2>
	<p>To exercise any of the rights described above, you may contact us through the contact form on our website. We may ask you to verify your identity before processing your request. You may also authorize an agent to act on your behalf, provided they supply the necessary documentation.</p>

	<hr />

	<h2>State-Specific Rights</h2>
	<p><strong>California residents:</strong> You have the right to opt out of the "sale" of your personal information as defined by the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA). You may also request, under the "Shine the Light" law, a list of categories of personal information shared with third parties for direct marketing purposes.</p>
	<p><strong>Colorado, Connecticut, Utah, and Virginia residents:</strong> You have the right to opt out of targeted advertising and to appeal any decision we make regarding your privacy rights. To exercise these rights, contact us through the form on our site.</p>

	<hr />

	<h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
	<p>We reserve the right to modify this Privacy Policy at any time. We will notify you of any significant changes by posting the new policy on this page with a revised update date. We encourage you to review this policy periodically.</p>

	<hr />

	<h2>How to Contact Us</h2>
	<p>If you have questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy or the handling of your personal information, you may contact us through our website. We will do our best to respond to your inquiry within a reasonable timeframe.</p>

